    "i2165": {
      "identifier": "ENG-2165",
      "title": "Refactor Roam Sync to use crossAppNodes",
      "description": "## Problem\n\n* We have two paths to write to the database: sync and publish. They use different converters, which violates DRY.\n* We want the sync to use the same CrossApp converters a publish.\n\n## Solution\n\n* Large-scale: Rewrite the sync to use the publish converters.\n  * To be broken down in sub-tasks\n* This is not code I think we should check in as-is, but Claude-generated code which I sent to help us understand the scope and surface.\n\n## Done When\n\n* The old sync path using RoamFullContentNode is removed.\n  * This will include [ENG-2061](https://linear.app/discourse-graphs/issue/ENG-2061/refactor-roamfullcontentnode-to-use-crossappnode-contract) \n* The sync path only upserts Concepts, with embedded Content, vs the two phases we have now.\n  * [ENG-1794](https://linear.app/discourse-graphs/issue/ENG-1794/atomic-upsert-of-concept-and-content) \n  * \n\n## Out of Scope\n\n* \n\n## Notes\n\n* We still need to handle the discrepancy between direct and direct_and_description\n  * Separate task but describing here\n  * Published nodes with isFirst child need both to be maintained by sync\n    * In sync, we can put the direct_and_description variant in the direct field of the Content (for isFirstChild nodes)\n    * And send the direct variant of published, isFirstChild nodes at sync, as a separate content upsert.\n  * Nodes without isFirstChild need only direct, so that is what sync will send.\n* I had Claude do this, thinking it appropriate while working on [ENG-2128](https://linear.app/discourse-graphs/issue/ENG-2128/express-source-as-a-sourcedocument-slotreference-of-evidence). It was decided that the testing would take too long, so it will be delayed. Still thinking it's worth examining the choices made while writing that code.\n* Here are some decision points identified by Claude while doing this.\n  * Investigation \u2014 why schema updates never landed\n    * Two independent sync paths, disagreeing: publishNodesToGroups used the cross-app converters but only inserted schemas missing from my_concepts; syncDgNodesToSupabase re-upserted schemas but through converters that emitted no slots and put template content under the template key that Obsidian reads as a template name.\n    * The server was never the constraint \u2014 upsert_concepts already does ON CONFLICT \u2026 DO UPDATE. Both gaps were client-side.\n    * nodeTypeSince misses child-block edits (it tests :edit/time on the type block, while format lives in a child). Still unfixed; it means schema changes reach the DB mainly via sharedNodeTypeIds.\n\n    sync-should-use-CrossApp\n    * Concept names preserved for block-backed nodes (\"{page title} {block text}\") \u2014 otherwise every such concept would be renamed against a unique (space_id, name) index.\n    * Variant became a property of the content, not of the slot it sits in \u2014 your design. That let the direct slot host a direct_and_description.\n    * Missing first child \u2192 plain direct \u2014 your call.\n    * The two-phase sync collapsed into one \u2014 your call, and it retired the withContents flag I'd added as a workaround. You read that flag correctly as a symptom.\n    * Embeddings only for changed nodes \u2014 a node present solely for a full-content backfill hasn't changed and keeps its own.\n    * CONCEPT_BATCH_SIZE 200 \u2192 50, since concepts now carry full page markdown.\n    * slot \u2192 defaultVariant \u2014 my rename collided with Concept.slots.\n    * RoamFullContentNode removed, and times declared number (option A) rather than widened to string | number \u2014 number is both narrower and true, since all three producers are datalog rows.\n    * Telemetry attribution shifts \u2014 markdown building moved into the getSharedFullContentUpdates phase; you accepted that.\n\n    Deferred, deliberately\n    * nodeTypeSince's blindness to child-block edits.\n    * A published isFirstChild node sending both a direct_and_description and a plain direct (recorded as a comment in roamToCrossAppConverters.ts).\n    * Producers returning CrossAppNode directly, together with folding node-type content into schema concepts \u2014 they share the upsertNodeSchemaToContent seam.",
      "state": {
        "name": "Icebox"
      },
      "project": {
        "name": "Post-V0 Roam\u2013Obsidian sync architecture"
      }
    },
    "i2166": {
      "identifier": "ENG-2166",
      "title": "Make upsertConcepts more like a PATCH than PUT",
      "description": "## Problem\n\n* When data is absent in a upsertConcepts, existing database data will be overwritten\n  * The way it was implemented did not allow to discern field absence\n  * As a consequence, different updating code paths need to agree fully.\n    * This was identified while comparing the sync and publish roam paths.\n\n## Solution\n\n* Make the upsertConcept more aware of missing fields, so it acts more like a PATCH than a PUT.\n\n## Done When\n\n* upsertConcept does not clobber absent values\n\n## Out of Scope\n\n* Changes to callers of upsertConcept\n\n## Notes\n\n* Right now, we treat reference_content and literal_content as a unit; we could decide to also make it an update, and use null as a sentinel delete value.\n* I had Claude do a first draft of this.\n* Here is a list of decision points\n  * Absent means preserve; explicit means clear. Defaults are applied before input in jsonb_populate_record, so absence was indistinguishable from empty by the time it reached the UPDATE.\n  * '' clears a description \u2014 jsonb has '{}' for that, text has only NULL, so an empty string became the escape hatch.\n  * author_id preserves on absent \u2014 your call: it should never legitimately be NULL.\n  * schema_id is erased only by declaring is_schema: true \u2014 your rule, rather than plain preserve.\n  * is_schema left alone \u2014 your call; making absence preserve there would shift semantics for every existing caller.\n  * Verification by rolled-back transaction, with a control run against main's functions proving the tests weren't passing vacuously.\n\nTODO: List specific fields.",
      "state": {
        "name": "Icebox"
      },
      "project": {
        "name": "Post-V0 Roam\u2013Obsidian sync architecture"
      }
    },
    "i1656": {
      "identifier": "ENG-1656",
      "title": "Rename folder for imported vault",
      "description": "## Problem\n\nThe imported vaults use the original vault name, which does not carry enough information.\n\n## Solution\n\nRename the folders inside `imported` from `{spaceName}` to `{owner-username}-{spaceName}`\n\nMay rely on imported folder `.dg.metadata` for folder identity\n\nWe should rename the folder when its original name is just the vault name.\n\nQuestion: If the user modifies the folder name of the imported vault afterwards, do we rename it back according to schema, or use the new name specified by the user (since we can rely on the `.dg.metadata` for folder identity)\n\n(I'm leaning towards the latter, and so does Trang.)\n\nMaybe we should have a migrated flag in the metadata, because what if they rename to vaultName?\n\n## Done When\n\nThe folders automatically get the new names.\n\n## Out of Scope\n\n\n\n## Notes",
      "state": {
        "name": "Ready for Review"
      },
      "project": {
        "name": "Obsidian within-lab DG collaboration (Publish & Import)"
      }
    },
    "i1972": {
      "identifier": "ENG-1972",
      "title": "Improve telemetry for imports and relation creation",
      "description": "## Problem\n\n* Weekly all-hands metrics cannot accurately report imported nodes/relations because import telemetry only captures `Import Dialog: Import Started`.\n* Relation telemetry is ambiguous: `Discourse Relation: Created` tracks relation type creation, while relation instance creation is only partially captured.\n* Publish/share telemetry is usable, but import and relation events need clearer names and completion counts.\n\n## Solution\n\n* Add `Import Dialog: Import Completed` after successful import with imported node/relation counts.\n* Add a confirmed relation-instance event after `createReifiedRelation` succeeds, including source surface where available.\n* Rename or replace `Discourse Relation: Created` with `Discourse Relation Type: Created` for relation schema/type creation.\n\n## Done When\n\n* PostHog taxonomy has separate events for relation type creation, confirmed relation instance creation, and completed imports with counts.\n* Weekly all-hands queries can report imported nodes/relations and relation instances without relying on started/triggered events.\n* Focused tests cover telemetry payload construction where practical.\n\n## Out of Scope\n\n* Building the Roam all-hands render or PostHog endpoint.\n* Backfilling historical PostHog events or rewriting existing dashboards.\n\n## Notes\n\n* Keep event names/properties stable for the future weekly comparison render.\n* Avoid sending sensitive graph/user content; prefer counts and low-risk metadata.",
      "state": {
        "name": "Draft"
      },
      "project": null
    },
    "i1878": {
      "identifier": "ENG-1878",
      "title": "Consolidate MVP0 cross-app fixtures for internal validation",
      "description": "## Problem\n\n* MVP0 fixtures may be scattered across contract, import, relation, and asset tickets.\n* Internal validation needs one predictable fixture set for tests and QA.\n\n## Solution\n\n* Consolidate Roam-origin and Obsidian-origin fixtures into a shared location.\n* Include markdown content, schema metadata, stable identity, relations, assets, and authorized/unauthorized access examples where available.\n* Reuse earlier fixtures instead of inventing incompatible sample data.\n\n## Done When\n\n* Tests and manual QA can reference one MVP0 fixture set.\n* Fixtures cover both Roam-origin and Obsidian-origin happy paths.\n* Known fixture limitations are documented.\n\n## Out of Scope\n\n* Creating new product behavior.\n* Replacing app-specific unit test fixtures that still serve narrower cases.\n* Full QA execution.\n\n## Notes\n\n* Functional requirement: [F15: Test and fixture coverage](<https://roamresearch.com/#/app/discourse-graphs/page/JLxa_X2HX>).\n* Depends on [ENG-1847](<https://linear.app/discourse-graphs/issue/ENG-1847/define-shared-cross-app-node-content-contract>), [ENG-1863](<https://linear.app/discourse-graphs/issue/ENG-1863/define-cross-app-relation-contract-and-fixtures>), and [ENG-1864](<https://linear.app/discourse-graphs/issue/ENG-1864/define-cross-app-asset-reference-contract>).\n* This should consolidate fixtures from Milestones 1-3 where possible.",
      "state": {
        "name": "Triage"
      },
      "project": {
        "name": "Post-V0 Roam\u2013Obsidian sync architecture"
      }
    }
  }
}
