{"id": "REL-13", "area": "REL", "title": "Cross-space relation published from Roam", "dirs": ["3S"], "steps": "Graph B imports node A1 from space A, relates it to its own B1, and publishes B1. Space C imports A1 and B1.", "expected": "C sees the A1–B1 relation as pending (last bug bash case, “test on eng-2202”).", "src": "UC6, last bug bash", "rating": "risk", "why": "Roam sends the imported page's local id as the endpoint. B's space has no record under that id, so the relation is rejected and not counted.", "ev": ["apps/roam/src/utils/roamToCrossAppConverters.ts:170-171", "apps/roam/src/utils/publishNodesToGroups.ts:163-166"], "method": "bash", "evidence": "shot", "pri": "P0"}
{"id": "REL-14", "area": "REL", "title": "Cross-space relation published from Obsidian", "dirs": ["3S"], "steps": "Vault B imports A1, relates it to B1, publishes B1. Space C imports A1 and B1.", "expected": "Same as REL-13.", "src": "UC6, last bug bash", "rating": "risk", "why": "Obsidian sends A1's origin id, but publishes the relation only when both notes list a shared group in frontmatter. Imported notes carry the source's groups by accident, and Roam-origin notes have none, so a Roam-origin A1 never works.", "ev": ["apps/obsidian/src/utils/publishNode.ts:101-130", "apps/obsidian/src/utils/importNodes.ts:1344-1365"], "method": "bash", "evidence": "shot", "pri": "P0"}
{"id": "REL-15", "area": "REL", "title": "Relation lands on the origin's own node", "dirs": ["3S"], "steps": "Continue REL-13 or REL-14: space A, which owns A1, imports B1.", "expected": "A sees the relation, pending, on its own A1.", "src": "UC6", "rating": "risk", "why": "Should work with Roam as A. With Obsidian as A, the relation is stored with the local id but the panel looks up imported ids only, so it shows on B1 and not on A1.", "ev": ["apps/obsidian/src/utils/relationsStore.ts:246-266, 441-463"], "method": "bash", "evidence": "shot", "pri": "P0"}
{"id": "REL-18", "area": "REL", "title": "Imported relation republished as local (Roam)", "dirs": ["3S"], "steps": "Get a pending imported relation between two of your own nodes (the reverse of REL-15), then publish one of those nodes.", "expected": "Imported relations, pending or accepted, aren't published as yours.", "src": "PR #1384 note", "rating": "risk", "why": "Publish filters on a key that Roam never writes, so imported relations whose endpoints are local nodes get published.", "ev": ["apps/roam/src/utils/publishNodesToGroups.ts:163-166"], "method": "bash", "evidence": "log", "pri": "P2"}
{"id": "SCH-09", "area": "SCH", "title": "Import preview vs result (Obsidian)", "dirs": ["RO", "OO"], "steps": "Import from a space whose type names differ only by case. Compare the preview with what's created.", "expected": "The preview matches the result.", "src": "Not specified", "rating": "risk", "why": "The preview matches exact names and the import matches case-insensitively. The relation count includes relations already present.", "ev": ["apps/obsidian/src/utils/importPreview.ts:112-114, 158-195"], "method": "bash", "evidence": "shot", "pri": "P2"}
{"id": "SCH-10", "area": "SCH", "title": "Two ways of creating node types disagree (Roam)", "dirs": ["RR", "OR"], "steps": "Import a relation whose endpoint type is missing, once with and once without first importing a node of that type.", "expected": "One type with the same format and id either way.", "src": "Not specified", "rating": "risk", "why": "Node import uses the source format and id; relation import uses a default “[[XXX]] - {content}” format and a random id.", "ev": ["apps/roam/src/utils/resolveSharedNodeTypes.ts:45-53", "apps/roam/src/utils/importSharedRelations.ts:56-75"], "method": "bash", "evidence": "shot", "pri": "P2"}
{"id": "RND-02", "area": "RND", "title": "Contribution round trip through a relation", "dirs": ["RR", "RO", "OR", "OO"], "steps": "A shares A1. B imports A1, creates B1 related to A1, and publishes B1. A imports B1. Run with each app as A and B.", "expected": "A sees the relation between its own A1 and the imported B1, pending.", "src": "UC6", "rating": "risk", "why": "See REL-13, REL-14 and REL-15: Roam as B drops the relation, and Obsidian as A shows it only on B1.", "ev": ["apps/roam/src/utils/roamToCrossAppConverters.ts:170-171", "apps/obsidian/src/utils/relationsStore.ts:246-266"], "method": "bash", "evidence": "shot", "pri": "P0"}
{"id": "UX-02", "area": "UX", "title": "Progress while relations import", "dirs": ["RR", "OR"], "steps": "Import several related nodes.", "expected": "Results show as soon as the nodes finish (the intent of commit b564f5c2).", "src": "ENG-2296", "rating": "risk", "why": "Progress is cleared only after relations finish, so the bar stays at “Importing N of N…” and the dialog can't close.", "ev": ["apps/roam/src/components/DiscoverSharedNodesDialog.tsx:339-362, 407"], "method": "bash", "evidence": "shot", "pri": "P1"}
{"id": "UX-03", "area": "UX", "title": "Relations error after every node failed", "dirs": ["RR", "OR"], "steps": "Make every selected node fail (for example with title collisions) while relations exist.", "expected": "No claim that nodes were imported.", "src": "ENG-2296", "rating": "risk", "why": "Relations run anyway, and the toast says “The nodes were imported, but their relations were not…”.", "ev": ["apps/roam/src/components/DiscoverSharedNodesDialog.tsx:339-348"], "method": "bash", "evidence": "shot", "pri": "P2"}
{"id": "UX-06", "area": "UX", "title": "Obsidian import notice counts", "dirs": ["RO", "OO"], "steps": "Import an Evidence whose Source comes along automatically, plus a node with a failing asset.", "expected": "The notice counts both nodes and mentions the asset problem.", "src": "ENG-1876", "rating": "risk", "why": "The automatic Source isn't counted and asset errors are never shown.", "ev": ["apps/obsidian/src/utils/importNodes.ts:1459-1465, 1785-1808"], "method": "bash", "evidence": "shot", "pri": "P2"}
{"id": "UX-07", "area": "UX", "title": "Space names in Obsidian", "dirs": ["RO", "OO"], "steps": "Open imported notes from a space you haven't listed in the import dialog since restarting.", "expected": "The real space name.", "src": "ENG-1876", "rating": "risk", "why": "Names are cached only when the dialog loads; otherwise the panel shows “Vault xxxxxxxx…” or a raw Roam URL.", "ev": ["apps/obsidian/src/components/ImportNodesModal.tsx:81-97", "apps/obsidian/src/utils/typeUtils.ts:57-60"], "method": "bash", "evidence": "shot", "pri": "P2"}
{"id": "SCL-03", "area": "SCL", "title": "More than 1,000 shared nodes", "dirs": ["RR", "RO", "OR", "OO"], "steps": "Make more than 1,000 nodes visible to one space.", "expected": "All of them are listed.", "src": "Not specified", "rating": "risk", "why": "Discovery isn't paginated, and the local database config caps a response at 1,000 rows. The production value isn't in the repo.", "ev": ["packages/database/src/lib/sharedNodes.ts:294-311", "packages/database/supabase/config.toml:18"], "method": "db", "evidence": "log", "pri": "P2"}
{"id": "SCL-04", "area": "SCL", "title": "Cleanup in a large space", "dirs": ["RR", "RO", "OR", "OO"], "steps": "A space with more than 1,000 rows (for Obsidian, about 500 nodes). Delete one node.", "expected": "It stops being shared.", "src": "Not specified", "rating": "risk", "why": "Orphan scans aren't paginated either, so deletions past the first 1,000 rows can be missed.", "ev": ["apps/roam/src/utils/cleanupOrphanedNodes.ts:12-17", "apps/obsidian/src/utils/syncDgNodesToSupabase.ts:67-90"], "method": "db", "evidence": "log", "pri": "P2"}
{"id": "SEC-01", "area": "SEC", "title": "Adding yourself to a space you don't belong to", "dirs": ["DB"], "steps": "Engineers only, on a local database: from one space's account, call the account-in-space function for a space it doesn't belong to.", "expected": "Refused.", "src": "Access model", "rating": "risk", "why": "Suspected from reading the SQL, not run. The function never checks membership, and LEAST ignores the NULL a non-member gets, which results in editor access.", "ev": ["packages/database/supabase/schemas/account.sql:228-237, 324-356"], "method": "db", "evidence": "log", "pri": "P0"}
{"id": "SEC-02", "area": "SEC", "title": "Joining through a group membership row", "dirs": ["DB"], "steps": "Engineers only, on a local database: insert a membership row whose group is an account that isn't a group yet. Also try rejoining a group everyone has left.", "expected": "Refused.", "src": "Access model", "rating": "risk", "why": "Suspected from reading the SQL, not run. The insert rule accepts any group id that has no members and never checks the member, and access is inherited through group ids.", "ev": ["packages/database/supabase/schemas/account.sql:216-224, 257-263, 586"], "method": "db", "evidence": "log", "pri": "P0"}
{"id": "SEC-04", "area": "SEC", "title": "Removing a group's space access", "dirs": ["DB"], "steps": "Delete G's space access on space A. As a member of G, read A's shared node from the tables and from storage.", "expected": "Nothing readable.", "src": "Access model", "rating": "risk", "why": "The views hide it, but tables and storage still allow reads through the per-node grant.", "ev": ["packages/database/supabase/schemas/content.sql:726", "packages/database/supabase/schemas/assets.sql:83-94"], "method": "db", "evidence": "log", "pri": "P1"}
{"id": "SEC-05", "area": "SEC", "title": "Overwriting a shared asset", "dirs": ["DB"], "steps": "As any signed-in space, overwrite an existing asset file, or upload under a hash before its owner does.", "expected": "Refused, or importers detect the mismatch.", "src": "Access model", "rating": "risk", "why": "Storage insert and update rules check only the bucket, and importers don't compare the bytes with the hash.", "ev": ["packages/database/supabase/schemas/assets.sql:134-157"], "method": "db", "evidence": "log", "pri": "P1"}
{"id": "SEC-06", "area": "SEC", "title": "Renaming another space", "dirs": ["DB"], "steps": "Call space creation with another space's URL and a wrong password, then check that space's name.", "expected": "The name doesn't change.", "src": "Access model", "rating": "risk", "why": "The space row is updated before the password check.", "ev": ["packages/database/supabase/functions/create-space/index.ts:77-117"], "method": "db", "evidence": "log", "pri": "P1"}

