1: // Titles arrive from other apps in their own syntax: Roam node titles carry page
2: // references ([[EVD]] - x - [[@Smith 2020]]) and tags. Obsidian creates a file with
3: // those characters in its name but cannot link to it, so references are unwrapped
4: // to keep the page name and the rest of the link characters (#^[]|, the set
5: // checkInvalidChars enforces on node type formats) are dropped with the OS set.
6: // A slash is dropped rather than made a folder: a Roam namespace and an Obsidian
7: // folder are not the same thing. Returns "" when nothing survives; the caller
8: // picks the fallback name.
9: const PAGE_REFERENCE = /\[\[([^\]]*)\]\]/g;
10: const REJECTED_IN_FILE_NAMES = /[<>:"/\\|?*#^[\]]/g;
